<h2 id="python" class="req req--action">Python</h2>
<p>Orcraft requires Python 3.14 or later, installed on <strong>both</strong> the controller
  machine and every endpoint machine.</p>
<p>New to Python? Download the installer from
  <a class="text-accent" href="https://www.python.org/downloads/">python.org</a>, run it, and make
  sure the "Add python.exe to PATH" option is checked during installation. Once installed, verify
  it from a terminal:</p>
{{ cmd.copyCommand("python --version") }}
<p>On Linux and macOS the command is usually <code>python3</code> rather than <code>python</code>.</p>

<h3 id="virtual-environment" class="req req--action">Virtual environment (recommended)</h3>
<p>A virtual environment keeps Orcraft isolated from the system Python, and avoids the
  <code>externally-managed-environment</code> message that recent distributions such as Ubuntu
  24.04 show for a plain <code>pip install</code>. Three commands:</p>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Step</th>
      <th>Windows</th>
      <th>Linux / macOS</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>Create</td>
      <td>{{ cmd.copyCell("python -m venv .venv") }}</td>
      <td>{{ cmd.copyCell("python3 -m venv .venv") }}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Activate</td>
      <td>{{ cmd.copyCell(".venv\\Scripts\\activate") }}</td>
      <td>{{ cmd.copyCell("source .venv/bin/activate") }}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Install</td>
      <td>{{ cmd.copyCell("pip install orcraft") }}</td>
      <td>{{ cmd.copyCell("pip install orcraft") }}</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>Activate the environment before running <code>orcraft-controller</code> or
  <code>orcraft-endpoint</code>. If PowerShell refuses to run the activation script, allow it for
  the current window only - no machine-wide change, no administrator rights:</p>
{{ cmd.copyCommand("Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned") }}

